  "final_message": "Implemented all three versions. Each scans lowercase words, resets the previous word at sentence-ending punctuation, counts adjacent pairs, and selects the top 20 using the specified tie order.\n\n- **Rust:** Uses word IDs, compact pair keys, and a fast hash table.\n- **plain.py:** Uses standard-library regular expressions and packed integer pair keys.\n- **fast.py:** Uses NumPy to aggregate packed pair IDs in bulk.\n\nAll three versions pass **s1, s2, and s3**. They also passed 26 edge and randomized cases. The final change to `plain.py` was followed by another pass of all three samples.",
